 29→ * {@link #longTermedBuilder()}, and {@link #segmentTermedBuilder()}.
 30→ *
 31→ * <h2>Composite key encoding</h2>
 32→ *
 33→ * <pre>
 34→ *   [4-byte big-endian term length][term bytes][doc-id bytes]
 35→ * </pre>
 36→ *
 37→ * All postings for the same term sort contiguously. A range scan for a term uses:
 38→ * <ul>
 39→ * <li>{@code scanStart = [termLen_be4][termBytes]} — sorts before all composite keys for this term
 40→ * because a prefix key sorts before any longer key with the same prefix under unsigned lex order
 41→ * <li>{@code scanEnd = incrementPrefix(scanStart)} — the lexicographic successor of the prefix;
 42→ * {@code null} on overflow → fall back to unbounded scan + prefix check in {@link DocIdIterator}
 43→ * </ul>
